# clips_fades_tempo_change (M3, TIME-001, TIME-007, DSP-001, D-06, DW-073): two adjacent clips
# with clip gain and linear fades, placed through a tempo map with a step change, move with the
# tempo but never stretch.
# assets/tone_441_48k.wav (gen_m3_assets.py) is a 441 Hz sine at 0.5, 35000 frames at the
# session rate. Clips A and B are added at 120 bpm, each 700 ticks (17500 frames, 25 per tick)
# so B continues the tone where A's audio stops: A plays source frames from 0 at gain 0.5 with
# fades 100/200 ticks, B from 17500 at gain 1.5 with fades 250/300. Then the tempo drops to
# 90 bpm at tick 240 (sample 6000, inside a 512-frame block, TIME-007): 33.33 frames per tick
# from there, so the ticks of both clips land later and their spans get longer (rounded with
# llround, 03 "Conversion semantics"):
#   A: [tickToSample(480), tickToSample(1180)) = [14000, 37333)   (at 120 bpm: [12000, 29500))
#      fade-in [14000, 17333), fade-out [30667, 37333)
#   B: [37333, 60667)                                                (at 120 bpm: [29500, 47000))
#      fade-in [37333, 45667), fade-out [50667, 60667)
# The audio isn't stretched: frame p of a clip plays source frame offset + (p - start). So A
# plays source frames 0..23332 (past the 17500 it was cut for), and B runs out of asset at
# 37333 + 17500 = 54833 and is silent for the rest of its span, inside its fade-out (D-06).
# Fades: frame k of a K-frame fade-in plays at k/K (0 on the clip's first frame), the fade-out
# mirrors it (DSP-001). Both strips are centre-panned: output = 0.5 · gain · fade · source.
# M3GoldenTests checks every sample against positions computed from DAWModel's TempoMap.
# @expect {"field": "frames", "value": 70000}
# @expect {"field": "firstNonSilentSample", "value": 14001}
# @expect {"field": "spectrumPeakHz", "value": 441, "tolerance": 6}
# @expect {"field": "peakDb", "value": -240, "range": {"start": 0, "end": 14001}}
# @expect {"field": "peakDb", "value": -18.062, "tolerance": 0.01, "range": {"start": 17333, "end": 30667}}
# @expect {"field": "peakDb", "value": -8.519, "tolerance": 0.01, "range": {"start": 45667, "end": 50667}}
# @expect {"field": "peakDb", "value": -240, "range": {"start": 54833, "end": 70000}}
project.new {"name": "clips_fades_tempo_change", "sampleRate": 48000}
command.apply {"command": {"type": "AddTrack", "name": "Clips", "kind": "audio"}}
asset.import {"path": "assets/tone_441_48k.wav"}
command.apply {"command": {"type": "AddClip", "trackID": 2, "start": 480, "length": 700, "assetID": 3, "gain": 0.5, "fadeIn": 100, "fadeOut": 200}}
command.apply {"command": {"type": "AddClip", "trackID": 2, "start": 1180, "length": 700, "assetID": 3, "sourceOffsetSamples": 17500, "gain": 1.5, "fadeIn": 250, "fadeOut": 300}}
command.apply {"command": {"type": "SetTempoEvent", "tick": 240, "bpm": 90}}
render.offline {"from": 0, "to": 2160, "path": "clips_fades_tempo_change.wav", "tail": false}
